---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use — Airbrush Learn"
  description="Terms of use for Airbrush Learn, a SprayGunner property."
  canonicalPath="/terms-of-use"
>
  <div class="pt-10 pb-16 mx-auto max-w-wide px-5">
    <div class="prose prose-site max-w-prose mx-auto">
      <h1 class="font-serif max-[640px]:text-[1.7rem]">Terms of Use</h1>
      <p><em>Last updated: August 23, 2026</em></p>
      <p>
        Airbrush Learn is published by SprayGunner. By using this site, you
        agree to the terms below.
      </p>

      <h2>Use of this site</h2>
      <p>
        Articles and content on Airbrush Learn are provided for general
        informational purposes about airbrushing techniques, equipment, and
        products. They are not professional, safety, or medical advice, and
        shouldn't be treated as a substitute for manufacturer instructions or
        professional guidance. You're welcome to reference and share our
        content for personal, non-commercial use; please credit Airbrush
        Learn and link back to the original article when you do.
      </p>

      <h2>Product mentions and links</h2>
      <p>
        Some articles link to SprayGunner's store and to manufacturer or
        informational sites. SprayGunner owns and operates Airbrush Learn, so
        links to spraygunner.com support the same business publishing this
        content. Product recommendations reflect our own editorial judgment
        and aren't guaranteed to be the right fit for your specific project.
      </p>

      <h2>Community gallery submissions</h2>
      <p>
        If you submit artwork through our
        <a href="/gallery/submit">community gallery</a>, you confirm that
        it's your own original work and that you have the right to share it.
        By submitting, you grant Airbrush Learn a non-exclusive,
        royalty-free, worldwide license to display, reproduce, and
        distribute your submission on this site, credited to the name you
        provide. You keep ownership and copyright of your work — this
        license doesn't take that away, and you're free to use or license
        your work elsewhere. We review every submission before it's
        published and may decline or remove a submission at our discretion.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you'd like a published piece removed, contact us (see below) and
        we'll take it down from the live site — note that a prior version
        may still exist in our public source code history, since that's how
        this site is built and maintained.
      </p>

      <h2>Prohibited use</h2>
      <p>
        Don't use this site to submit content that isn't yours, that's
        unlawful, or that infringes someone else's rights. Don't attempt to
        disrupt, scrape at scale, or interfere with the site's normal
        operation.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms as the site evolves. The "Last updated"
        date above reflects the most recent revision.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms can be directed to us through
        <a href="https://spraygunner.com/">spraygunner.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
